1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:10,731
It's Easter morning. I'm awake, but I
stay in bed. There's nothing to look

2
00:00:10,731 --> 00:00:12,282
forward to.

3
00:00:12,782 --> 00:00:21,530
For me, every holiday is the same. At
our house, Mom makes the food and leaves

4
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:22,539
for work.

5
00:00:23,039 --> 00:00:29,415
It's just me, my dad and my brother at
home. The only thing that makes it

6
00:00:29,415 --> 00:00:33,694
different from any other day is the
special food.

7
00:00:34,194 --> 00:00:42,694
Lying in bed, I think I hear my mother's
voice. I get up to check.

8
00:00:42,744 --> 00:00:49,718
I walk out, and my mother is home.
Sitting on a little stool, making

9
00:00:49,718 --> 00:00:50,436
coffee.

10
00:00:50,486 --> 00:00:57,007
There's fresh green grass on the floor.
Incense burns beside the coffee.

11
00:00:57,507 --> 00:01:04,495
Holiday music is playing. My dad and
brother are getting the lamb ready.

12
00:01:04,995 --> 00:01:12,186
The coffee Mom is roasting and the
incense fill the house. Standing in the

13
00:01:12,186 --> 00:01:16,753
doorway watching them, I've never been
happier.

14
00:01:17,253 --> 00:01:27,182
This is the first holiday I remember
spending with my mother. To this day,

15
00:01:27,182 --> 00:01:31,610
it's the happiest day of my life.

16
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:37,011
More than anything, showing up matters.
